      "start": 0.58,
      "end": 2.69,
      "text": "Hey, how's it going? You doing okay?"
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 9.53,
      "end": 18.44,
      "text": "Split the logs to get at the dry wood inside, and start with lots of small dry kindling. Birch bark or a few cotton balls with petroleum jelly catch really well."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 22.25,
      "end": 26.61,
      "text": "It does. They burn for a few minutes, which gives the damp twigs time to dry and catch."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 34.0,
      "end": 40.25,
      "text": "Small is better for cooking. A compact bed of hot coals heats a pot much more evenly than big flames."
    },
    {
      "kind": "reply",
      "start": 46.66,
      "end": 52.47,
      "text": "Drown it with water, stir the ashes, and drown it again. If it's still warm to the back of your hand, keep going."
    }
  ]
